{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639978-demon-translations-vs-mage-frommage-the-ascension","id":639978,"title":"Demon translations vs Mage frommage the ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-26T02:06:01-07:00","id":639978,"title":"Demon translations vs Mage frommage the ascension","content":"I wanted to know how does a translated god machine demon defend them self from a Mage ?<br /> <br /> How does it work to defend from there spells ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T03:58:16-07:00","id":640041,"title":"","content":"Hello, <br /> <br /> In the same manner as any other supernatural creature does: with their power stat Primum, or in case of demons with Cover if they are, well, in cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T17:16:29-07:00","id":640834,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're using M20 rules, you'd probably use the sidebar with night-folk defenses, applying Cover as the dice cap for counterspelling. The rest probably depends on what Embeds and Exploits they have. The Look, as usual, would be pretty powerful depending on the mage's paradigm and foci. In general, demonic powers aren't specifically geared to counter magick as opposed to any other supernatural threat, but have the potential for clever use to mess with the weight of consensus and a particular mage's paradigm, if the demon knows to try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T20:04:34-07:00","id":641016,"title":"","content":"I just have one player saying there is no defense to mage magic if your not a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T21:12:22-07:00","id":641053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639978-demon-translations-vs-mage-frommage-the-ascension?p=641016#post641016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have one player saying there is no defense to mage magic if your not a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by NWoD raw that's blatantly untrue. Anything supernatural that is resisted/contested is resisted/contested by any given supernatural creature's Supernatural Tolerance (Primum, Blood Potency, Gnosis, etc etc.) Plus Demons have that extra advantage of using Cover as resistance when they're wearing said Cover.<br /> <br /> Of course, it depends on what mechanics you're using - are you playing Ascension mechanics and backporting Demons (using the Translation guide?), or are you playing Ascension using NWoD 1/2 mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T21:16:26-07:00","id":641055,"title":"","content":"That's more of a Mage thing than a Demon thing, owing to the way that cWoD games focus more on their own template rather than plan more for crossover interactions. I think there was a Storyteller's Handbook a few years before the Time of Judgment that had chapters on crossover resolutions? But it's all very fiddly and exception-based rather than much in the way of universal rules, and really comes down to the Storyteller's decision as to what works for his game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}